Lay out a three- or four-component 64-bit vector varying in two locations for GLSL and SPIR-V.

DefaultVaryingLayoutRulesImpl::GetVectorLayout (source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp) gives every
vector one varying slot, with a TODO noting that vectors of double may need other handling. The
Vulkan specification ("Location Assignment") and GLSL 4.60 (4.4.1) give a three- or
four-component vector of a 64-bit type two consecutive locations. For a vertex input
`float3 position; double4 wide; float2 after;` Slang assigns locations 0, 1 and 2, decorates the
SPIR-V to match, and reports the same in reflection; with the validation layer,
vkCreateShaderModule reports VUID-StandaloneSpirv-OpEntryPoint-08721, "conflicting input location
assignment at location 2, component 0".

This gives GLSLVaryingLayoutRulesImpl, used for the GLSL and SPIR-V targets, a GetVectorLayout
that returns two slots for a 64-bit vector of more than two components. A regression test is
added as tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-wide-vertex-input-locations.cpp. This is Slang issue
#13427.

Measured on v2026.21: locations 0, 1, 2 for the inputs above, in the module and in reflection, on
all four platforms.
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp b/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp
index 3b6cfd40f..1af403475 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp
@@ -1051,6 +1051,28 @@ struct GLSLVaryingLayoutRulesImpl : DefaultVaryingLayoutRulesImpl
         : DefaultVaryingLayoutRulesImpl(kind)
     {
     }
+
+    SimpleLayoutInfo GetVectorLayout(
+        BaseType elementType,
+        SimpleLayoutInfo elementInfo,
+        size_t elementCount) override
+    {
+        // A three- or four-component vector of a 64-bit type consumes two consecutive locations
+        // ("Location Assignment" in the Vulkan specification; GLSL 4.60 4.4.1).
+        //
+        switch (elementType)
+        {
+        case BaseType::Double:
+        case BaseType::Int64:
+        case BaseType::UInt64:
+            if (elementCount > 2)
+                return SimpleLayoutInfo(getKind(), 2);
+            break;
+        default:
+            break;
+        }
+        return DefaultVaryingLayoutRulesImpl::GetVectorLayout(elementType, elementInfo, elementCount);
+    }
 };
 
